  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves analyzing the evolution of popular music from 1964 to 2018 using data from both Billboard charts and Spotify. The goal is to understand trends in music popularity and identify influential artists, albums, and songs. This analysis includes examining musical attributes and their correlations with song popularity. An interactive Tableau Dashboard will be implemented for data exploration.\n\nObjectives\n\n1. Identify and analyze trends in music over time.\n2. Determine the most influential artists, albums, and songs.\n3. Examine correlations between musical attributes and song popularity.\n4. Provide interactive data visualizations through a Tableau Dashboard.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Music analysts and researchers.\n- Music industry professionals and historians.\n- General public interested in music trends and history.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Analysis: \n   - Analyze Billboard chart data and Spotify musical elements to identify trends.\n   - Compare and contrast attributes of top-charting songs and other hits.\n\n2. Data Visualization:\n   - Develop an interactive Tableau Dashboard to explore findings.\n\n3. Reporting:\n   - Generate reports identifying influential artists, albums, and trends.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Performance:\n   - The system should efficiently handle large datasets from 1964 to 2018.\n\n2. Usability:\n   - The Tableau Dashboard should be user-friendly and intuitive for all users.\n\n3. Scalability:\n   - Design should accommodate future data expansion beyond 2018.\n\n4. Security:\n   - Ensure the secure handling of any sensitive data or user information.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0189\nCREATE TABLE `artists` (\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `active_start_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `active_end_year` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`artist_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `albums` (\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `album_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `label_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`album_id`),\n  KEY `artist_id` (`artist_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `albums_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`artist_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `songs` (\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `album_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `song_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `duration_ms` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`song_id`),\n  KEY `artist_id` (`artist_id`),\n  KEY `album_id` (`album_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `songs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`artist_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `songs_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`album_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `billboard_charts` (\n  `chart_entry_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `chart_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `chart_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `rank_position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weeks_on_chart` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`chart_entry_id`),\n  KEY `song_id` (`song_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `billboard_charts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`song_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `spotify_tracks` (\n  `spotify_track_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `spotify_track_uri` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `popularity` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `danceability` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `energy` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `key_signature` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `loudness` decimal(6,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `mode` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `speechiness` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `acousticness` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `instrumentalness` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `liveness` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `valence` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tempo` decimal(7,3) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`spotify_track_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `spotify_track_uri` (`spotify_track_uri`),\n  KEY `song_id` (`song_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `spotify_tracks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`song_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `dashboard_reports` (\n  `report_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `report_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `report_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
